nt_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:08194b2dcff916f404f501a00bf6a7f00b32c15fabebc228553a3bb559646a33","file":"preprints/Critical-mixing-in-the-Sherrington-Kirkpatrick-model-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":54,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"2d7455fae806375b110f65e6c5db416af3da34f260ee8abcfd7d81346766465e","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Critical-mixing-in-the-Sherrington-Kirkpatrick-model-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:08194b2dcff916f404f501a00bf6a7f00b32c15fabebc228553a3bb559646a33","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Critical-mixing-in-the-Sherrington-Kirkpatrick-model-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L54"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor every fixed $\\varepsilon\\in(0,1/2)$, in probability over the Gaussian\ndisorder,\n\\begin{align*}\n t_{\\mathrm{mix},J}(\\varepsilon)&=n^{2/3+o(1)},&\n k_{\\mathrm{mix},J}(\\varepsilon)&=n^{5/3+o(1)},\\\\\n R_J&=n^{2/3+o(1)},& C_{\\mathrm{LS},J}&=n^{2/3+o(1)}.\n\\end{align*}\nIn each expression, $X_n=n^{a+o(1)}$ means that for every fixed\n$\\delta>0$, $\\Pprob\\{n^{a-\\delta}\\le X_n\\le n^{a+\\delta}\\}\\to1$."}
